## 7. Daily Stories System

Implement a polished, fully functional stories feature.

### Stories interface

Display a horizontally scrollable row of circular profile images near the top of the home feed.

Include:
- Add Story.
- The current user's story.
- Stories from followed or connected professionals.
- An unread indicator.
- A viewed indicator.
- Clear visual distinction between viewed and unviewed stories.

Use circular profile images, subtle borders, consistent sizing, and clear labels.

Remove the oversized “DOCTOR STORIES” banners, unnecessary expiry countdown banners, and excessive story-card decoration if they exist in the current design.

The story row should feel natural and compact, not like a separate oversized dashboard.

### Publishing a story

When the user clicks Add Story, open a polished story composer.

Support the media types that the existing backend and product requirements can safely support:
- Image.
- Video.
- Text-based status.
- Optional educational or professional caption.

Provide:
- Media preview.
- Caption input.
- Audience/privacy selection.
- Cancel.
- Publish Story.
- Upload progress.
- Success and error feedback.

Validate file type and size. Display meaningful errors when uploads fail.

### Story lifecycle

- Stories should be publishable every day.
- Each published story should expire 24 hours after publication.
- Expired stories must not appear as active stories.
- The backend must enforce expiry; hiding expired stories only in the frontend is insufficient.
- Record publication time and expiry time.
- Update unread/viewed states appropriately.
- Allow authorized users to delete their own stories.
- Allow users to view their own active stories.
- Provide a story viewer with next/previous navigation, progress indicators, pause/resume behavior where supported, and a close button.
- Make the viewer usable on desktop and mobile.
- Provide appropriate keyboard and accessibility support.

Do not display a constantly visible expiry countdown on the home feed. Show expiry information inside the story viewer or story management interface when useful.

Do not automatically delete permanent posts when stories expire.

### Story privacy

Only show stories to audiences permitted by the user's privacy settings and relationship rules.

Do not expose private stories or private profile data through public API endpoints.

